            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThe only way I could reproduce this is if there is a `MiniDeps.add()` call executed during startup which leads to installing a plugin. And it doesn't depend on color scheme but on the implementation of `vim.notify` (which is universally used in 'mini.deps' to show these messages). Everything works as expected in case of an interactive `:DepsAdd`.\r\n\r\n My suggestion would be to use a more robust implementation of `vim.notify`. Like, for example, is suggested in ['mini.deps' example 'init.lua'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/691c5f38f575b572d0c857bd22c35be9a1512925/scripts/init-deps-example.lua#L24-L27).\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue (either of 'mini.base16' or 'mini.deps').",
